## Sanity — public (safe to expose in the browser bundle)
PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID="rkp7m27a"
PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET="production"

## Visual Editing.
## When "true", Astro builds in server mode, fetches draft content and renders
## the click-to-edit overlays. Leave this OFF (or unset) for the production
## deploy so the live site stays static and stega-free.
PUBLIC_SANITY_VISUAL_EDITING_ENABLED="false"

## Server-only — never prefix with PUBLIC_. Required whenever Visual Editing
## is enabled, since draft content needs an authenticated read.
## Create one at https://www.sanity.io/manage/project/rkp7m27a/api#tokens
SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN=""

## Which deployment the Studio's Preview tab loads in its iframe.
## Leave unset locally — "same-origin" means astro dev, which is what you want.
## On the PRODUCTION deploy set this to the preview deployment's URL, because
## production itself is static and has drafts turned off.
# PUBLIC_SANITY_PREVIEW_ORIGIN="https://preview.iicon.pages.dev"
